*Blocker:* a path beyond the one; a changed byte in `journey.ts`, the config, the scripts, `.github`, `package*.json` or `src`; a budget VALUE, an existing `expect`, or the 7-minute total changed; **any browser navigation or browser-originated request before `t0`** (a browser-side warm-up changes what the first span times: the option the builder kit forbade); plant p1 or p2 left GREEN with the warm-up in place; a new cookie from the warm-up that changes the sign-in (STOP, tier 1); a walked route that is not warmed and sits under a budgeted span with a measured cost above 100 ms; a request to any origin other than your loopback ports; a run of yours that binds 3100 or 3597-3599; a secret; a person's name, card id or `B###` token in an added line or message; a reproduced red (3 of 3 alone) at head not at main; the head moved; a NEW CodeQL alert at or above the ruleset's thresholds. *Major (class "the measurement hides a slow step"):* p3 (slow server render on every request) left GREEN where the route is dynamic; a span that ROSE by more than 300 ms hosted AND locally reproduced because of the warm-up; the builder's counts contradicted with a verdict consequence; a failing required check. *Minor/Note:* p4 masked (by design, matches the stated intent) -- a Note, never a finding to fix, with both runs printed; the rise of `submit + score` if noise; "no assertion" wording; the walked-not-warmed route under no span; a one-run hosted sample; the bimodal local first span; unsigned commit; trailer; CodeQL PENDING at the verdict; runner differences you cannot run. Say which rule you applied for every finding. **Round 1 of 2: do not pad a Note into a NO GO and do not soften a Blocker: quote the plant, the row and the number.** **VERDICT RULES.** GO needs C1-C4, C6 and C8 measured with their controls, p1 and p2 red, c0/c1/c-fail fired, p5 flagged by the C2 instrument, zero findings above Note, every `Analyze (<language>)` COMPLETE with the PR's open alerts zero (control fired) and every required context `success`; GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note/Condition only; NO GO on any Blocker or Major, with the class named, "round 1 of 2" and the fix-shape in prose. A security-shaped finding you cannot classify is a STOP.
